{"clips": [
  {
    "id": "C1",
    "weakest_point": "The first 3 seconds are a static close-up and a cryptic warning with no action; the ad also ends on Alexander's reaction after the thorn-stabbing peak has passed.",
    "hook": {
      "score": 2,
      "reason": "Above the 3-s line there is only a close-up of a scarred face and the line 'They will tear your hands apart.' It is ominous but gives a scroller no action or context to stop for."
    },
    "cliffhanger": {
      "score": 2,
      "reason": "It ends on Alexander crying 'Please... enough!' after Juliana has already been stabbed by the thorns; the conflict has peaked and this is a reaction, not an unresolved cut."
    },
    "questions": [
      {"q": "Will Juliana find the object that secures Alexander's freedom?", "type": "intrigue"},
      {"q": "Why is Alexander chained and who are the nobles on the balcony?", "type": "confusion"}
    ],
    "standalone": {
      "score": 4,
      "reason": "You can see the cruel nobles, the wronged couple, and the stakes (his freedom, her safety), though the exact object is not named until late."
    },
    "emotion": {
      "score": 4,
      "reason": "The villains' gloating and Juliana's sacrificial crawl through frozen thorns create a strong sense of injustice and dread."
    },
    "want_next": {
      "score": 3,
      "reason": "The scenario is engaging, but the slow 60-second build risks losing scrollers before the payoff."
    },
    "ad_policy": {
      "level": "mild",
      "category": "violence",
      "reason": "Visible blood, thorns raking across skin, and bloody wounded hands."
    },
    "one_line_verdict": "A clear, emotionally heavy setup that starts too slowly and ends on a reaction."
  },
  {
    "id": "C2",
    "weakest_point": "It drops the viewer directly into mid-action with no setup; the first 3 seconds are pure pain without explaining why Juliana is crawling through thorns.",
    "hook": {
      "score": 5,
      "reason": "The ad opens on Juliana screaming 'Ahhh!' as branches lacerate her arm and cheek; the shock and blood land in the first second with no context needed."
    },
    "cliffhanger": {
      "score": 4,
      "reason": "It cuts to black on a macro shot of her bloody fist closing around the emerald ring; the search resolves, but whether the ring saves Alexander is left open."
    },
    "questions": [
      {"q": "Will the emerald ring actually secure Alexander's freedom?", "type": "intrigue"},
      {"q": "Why is Juliana being forced to dig for a ring in the thorns?", "type": "confusion"}
    ],
    "standalone": {
      "score": 3,
      "reason": "Followable as a bloody woman forced to dig for a ring while a man is restrained, but the relationship and full stakes require inference."
    },
    "emotion": {
      "score": 4,
      "reason": "Immediate visceral pain and desperation give a gut-punch; the ring discovery delivers a fierce, painful triumph."
    },
    "want_next": {
      "score": 4,
      "reason": "Finding the ring creates a strong need to see if it works and whether she survives."
    },
    "ad_policy": {
      "level": "mild",
      "category": "violence",
      "reason": "Visible blood, facial lacerations, and bloody hands scraping the ground."
    },
    "one_line_verdict": "A punchy, visceral mid-action cut that hooks instantly but sacrifices setup."
  }
],
  "best": "C2",
  "best_why": "C2 stops the scroll in the first second with a scream and blood, while C1 wastes the critical opening 3 seconds on a static close-up and ends after the peak."
}
